From 4a8ae17125c6b2276c87a5d51b44a77879b3c464 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:25:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] test(remote notices): pin _task_rows own-gateway
 exclusion and planner order

Post-merge mutation check of #2409 (card t_01a1d5f0a7c905e0): two mutants of
tui_gateway/kanban_remote_notices._task_rows survived the 11 remote notice suites.

- C08: dropping `gw != ?` (an unfiltered `coll = 'tasks'` read) lets this gateway's
  own cards into the no-seq observation path (kanban_remote_observations._snapshot),
  which does not filter them itself. Pinned by a direct `_task_rows(conn, "A")` test
  and by the observation snapshot test.
- C07: returning identities re-sorted by rowid instead of the identity query's order.
  With the hub's (coll, gw, seq) index the planner order differs from rowid order;
  cold reads must list cards in the same order as warm reads
  (remote_index_projection._read_rows runs the same identity query), as the docstring
  promises. The fixture asserts the two orders differ so the test stays discriminating.

Proof (scripts/run_tests.sh tests/tui_gateway/test_task_rows_own_gateway_and_order.py):
main 3 passed; C08 3 failed; C07 1 failed (the order test).
